    question_en: "SkyHop Airlines operates a regional flight booking and ticketing platform running on Amazon EC2 instances and container images stored in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Following a recent security audit, a solutions architect must improve the platform's security posture while minimizing operational overhead.\n\nThe security team has established two key requirements:\n- Continuously and automatically detect known software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and unintended network exposure across EC2 instances and container images stored in ECR without managing custom assessment agents.\n- Continuously analyze VPC Flow Logs, DNS query logs, and AWS CloudTrail management events to intelligently identify potential threats—such as anomalous API activity, communication with known malicious IPs, and compromised EC2 instances—without installing host-level software agents.\n\nWhich combination of AWS services should the solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
