    question_en: "A mobile game studio is launching a new multiplayer game and is designing its backend architecture on AWS. The game requires a custom session management service hosted on Linux-based virtual servers to handle active player sessions. The studio anticipates unpredictable traffic spikes during marketing campaigns and weekends. Additionally, after each match finishes, the mobile client uploads game telemetry logs and match results (each taking less than 30 seconds to parse) directly to an Amazon S3 bucket. The studio needs an automated, event-driven solution to parse these logs, validate match results, and update leaderboard data with minimal operational overhead and no idle compute costs.\n\nWhich architecture should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements?",
