      "Store the configuration parameters and encrypted database credentials in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as standard and SecureString parameters. Grant read permissions to the Lambda function execution role and the EC2 IAM instance profile. Use AWS Systems Manager Session Manager to allow administrators to access the private EC2 instances without opening inbound ports.",
      "Store the configuration parameters and credentials in local configuration files baked into a custom Amazon Machine Image (AMI) for the EC2 instances, and configure environment variables on the Lambda function. Use AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager to distribute configuration updates and manage remote administrative SSH access to the private EC2 instances.",
