    question_en: "A digital healthcare startup is developing an automated pipeline to process patient medical intake records uploaded to an Amazon S3 bucket. The workflow requires several sequential steps: validating document metadata, extracting text and anonymizing protected health information (PHI), routing records with low confidence scores to human clinicians for manual review (which can take up to 48 hours), and writing the finalized records to an Amazon DynamoDB table.\n\nCurrently, the development team has implemented direct point-to-point invocations between AWS Lambda functions, but they are facing issues managing retries, tracking execution state, and handling multi-day human review delays. A solutions architect needs to redesign the architecture to minimize operational overhead, eliminate custom retry logic, and avoid paying for idle compute during the human review stage.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements?",
