    question_en: "A company is migrating a containerized application from an on-premises environment to AWS. The application processes incoming data files, and each job takes between 25 and 45 minutes to finish. The application must securely read from and write to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company wants to minimize operational overhead and avoid provisioning or managing underlying server infrastructure.\n\nWhich combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
