    question_en: "An insurance company processes large volumes of policyholder claims daily. The company runs a core claims analytics and underwriting workload in an Amazon VPC, which must securely interact with legacy on-premises claims databases. During normal business hours, the integration requires dedicated, consistent network performance, high bandwidth, and predictable low latency for real-time adjustor lookups and large document transfers.\n\nThe company requires an automated failover mechanism to maintain hybrid connectivity in case the primary network path fails. However, to optimize operational expenses, management does not want to provision a redundant physical connection for backup purposes.\n\nWhich network architecture will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
