    question_en: "A healthcare startup is designing an architecture to process and store digitized patient intake records. Clinics upload records throughout the day, and an overnight batch processing application on Amazon EC2 extracts clinical metadata and writes the results to an Amazon S3 bucket. The batch workload pulls tasks from an Amazon SQS queue, and jobs are stateless and can be safely interrupted and resumed without data loss.\n\nThe processed files in Amazon S3 are accessed frequently by clinical staff during the first 30 days. Between day 31 and day 90, requests drop substantially to only a few times per month. After 90 days, the files are rarely accessed, but regulatory compliance mandates that all records must be retained for 7 years and be retrievable within 3 to 5 hours when requested for audits.\n\nWhich combination of actions will meet these requirements MOST cost-effectively?",
