    question_en: "A company hosts a web application on Amazon EC2 instances that connects to an Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL database. To comply with internal security policies, the company must meet the following requirements:\n• Database credentials must not be hardcoded in application code, must be encrypted at rest using an encryption key that the company can audit and manage, and must be automatically rotated every 30 days.\n• All network traffic between the EC2 instances and the RDS database must be encrypted in transit.\n\nWhich combination of actions should a solutions architect recommend to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)",
