    question_en: "A company receives data files uploaded by external partners into an Amazon S3 bucket throughout the day. Each file is smaller than 50 MB, and processing takes approximately 30 to 45 seconds per file. File uploads are sporadic, with unpredictable spikes and long periods of inactivity. As soon as a file is uploaded, it must be validated and transformed, with the extracted metadata saved to an Amazon DynamoDB table. In addition, the raw files in the S3 bucket must be automatically deleted 30 days after upload to reduce storage costs.\n\nWhich solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?",
