    question_en: "A real-estate technology company hosts an online property listing platform on AWS. The architecture consists of an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances running the web application in public subnets, and an Amazon RDS for MySQL Multi-AZ DB cluster in private subnets.\n\nDuring a security review, the operations team identified that a specific external CIDR block (198.51.100.0/24) is aggressively scraping listing data and must be immediately blocked from accessing the web application. In addition, company security policy requires that the database tier must only accept incoming connections on port 3306 from the web application instances, following the principle of least privilege and adapting automatically when web instances scale in or out without requiring manual IP address updates.\n\nWhich combination of configurations will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead?",
