    question_en: "A fintech company is designing the network architecture for a payment processing platform deployed on Amazon EC2 instances across two Availability Zones (AZs) in an Amazon VPC. The EC2 instances reside in private subnets and must not accept inbound connections from the internet.\n\nThe architecture must meet the following requirements:\n- The EC2 instances must securely initiate outbound HTTPS connections to external banking APIs over the internet.\n- The instances frequently archive high volumes of transaction receipts to an Amazon S3 bucket within the same AWS Region.\n- The architecture must remain highly available and fault-tolerant against a single AZ outage.\n- Data transfer and processing costs must be optimized with minimal operational overhead.\n\nWhich solution should a solutions architect recommend to satisfy these requirements?",
